WHAT: move KCrash unconditional find_package(Qt6Test REQUIRED) inside
      if(BUILD_TESTING).
WHY:  the call sits at TOP-LEVEL scope (CMakeLists.txt:37), not inside the
      `if(BUILD_TESTING)` block twenty lines below -- so even a
      -DBUILD_TESTING=OFF build demands it. wk qtbase is FEATURE_testlib=OFF
      (plugins/qt/build-qtbase.sh), so this is a hard configure failure for a
      package the LIBRARY never uses: Qt6::Test appears in zero link lines
      under src/. It serves the autotests alone.
      SEPARATE, AND IMPORTANT: this patch makes KCrash BUILD. It does not make
      crash handling work, and it cannot -- KCrash handler re-execs the
      process and forks drkonqi, and there is no fork on WASI. The app
      therefore does NOT call KCrash::initialize(); see the comment in KCalc
      main.cpp patch, which says so out loud rather than leaving it looking
      like an oversight.
UPSTREAM: as-is. This is a plain bug in their tree -- any Qt build without
      testlib hits it, wasm or not.
diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index cce6e90..d0d9cf9 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -34,7 +34,15 @@ if(WITH_X11)
     find_package(X11 REQUIRED)
     set(HAVE_X11 TRUE)
 endif()
-find_package(Qt6Test ${REQUIRED_QT_VERSION} CONFIG REQUIRED)
+# Qt6Test is required at TOP-LEVEL scope here, not inside the
+# `if(BUILD_TESTING)` further down at line 70 -- so a -DBUILD_TESTING=OFF
+# build still demands it. wk's qtbase is FEATURE_testlib=OFF (see
+# plugins/qt/build-qtbase.sh), so this is a hard configure failure for a
+# package nothing in the LIBRARY uses: grep KF6Crash's src/ and Qt6::Test
+# appears in exactly zero link lines. It serves the autotests alone.
+if(BUILD_TESTING)
+    find_package(Qt6Test ${REQUIRED_QT_VERSION} CONFIG REQUIRED)
+endif()
 include(ECMGenerateExportHeader)
 include(ECMSetupVersion)
 include(ECMGenerateHeaders)
